  "text": "18-K. 2. During the years 1981 and 1982 and 1983, an employee may elect to accumulate any or all of his unused leave days. To elect this option, the employee must notify in writing the office of the employer by November 1 of each of the above years that he is accumulating such leave. Annually, on or before November 1, at the request of an employee, the office shall provide a signed statement of paid leave days which have been accumulated by that employee. Such accumulated Jeave can be taken at any time during the term of this Agreement and will be paid at the then prevailing rate. Accumulated leave not taken during the term of this Agreement shall be liquidated and payment, at the prevailing rate, made within 80 days following the expiration of the Agreement, unless there is mutual agreement to continue accumulated leave for a later date. If leave days are not accumulated, the employee shall receive, on the pay day of the first pay period in December of that year, the cash payment for any such days he has not taken in that calendar year. The Union recognizes the need for sufficient manpower for the efficient operation of the publishers in connection with the use of accumulated leave time in excess of ten days, The Union agrees that such accumulated leave shall not be taken in such a manner as to interfere with adequate staffing."
