  "text": "SECTION 17 Mutual Guarantees i7-A.1. Because of the enactment of the Labor- Management Relations Act, 1947, this contract ‘differs from contracts between these parties over a period of many years. Specifically, this agreement eliminates the closed shop, and references thereto because it no longer is permissible under the federal law. This provision is printed below in italics for reference only and not as a part of this Agreement. 2-L. The Union shall furnish at all times and at regular time rates as many men as may be required by a Publisher, such men to be comtion for which they are required. If a Publisher requires his regular employees to work in excess of a fifth shift, overtime at the rate of time and one-half shall be paid for the full shift. When 68 + Me _the Union fails to furnish such men prompily, the Publisher is authorized to meet his needs by employing such men as he may be able to obtain; tf the men so employed are not members of the Union they shall be employed only so long as the Union does not furnish members of the Union willing and qualified to take their places, but any man so employed shall be allowed to complete his day’s work. Nothing herein contained is to be construed as conferring power upon any Publisher to fill a regular situation with anyone not a member of the Union."
