  "id": "c252",
  "name": "22-A. Times Carlstadt Facility — General Memorandum",
  "text": "SECTION 22 SHOP CONDITIONS: THE TIMES Times Carlstadt Facility 22-A. These are the final minutes of The Times-NMDU Sub-Committee. These Minutes are divided into three main chapters: I—General Memorandum Concerning Carlstadt; J]—Jurisdiction at Carlstadt; and J]]-—Over-the-Road Trucking. . The Times and the Union agree as set forth below on certain aspeets of The Times’ operations at its new facility at Carlstadt, New Jersey. Two major factors in the decision of The Times to make the large capital investment re- . Gaired by the Carlstadt facility were the need ‘go make substantial productivity gains and to meet the competitive challenge of suburban newspapers. The partics recognize that the challenge of suburban newspapers can be met only if the production and distribution of The Times are timely and meet the needs of the reader. Accordingly, The Times and the Union commit themselves to-the achievement of maximum productivity and efficiency at the Carlstadt facility consistent with the terms of this memorandum and of the contract. This does not preclude the Union from negotiating for manning that is hecessary to perform the various tasks in its jurisdiction and to avoid undue hardships. 85 FUNDO000967 : fe “gto * + *, « . “ et ata dees faite bbe toe ine Wet em te lee em ee a 4 ” AM a, ee Te . 2 ) eat The Times and the Union note their commitment to the orderly settlement of disputes that arise during the term of the contract (as set forth in Section 16 of the contract) and affirm that any disputes that arise between them at the Carlstadt facility will be resolved expeditiously and without interruption of operations."
},
